1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hittade moster Lallas forskning "Om karolinen Robert Petre". Skall försöka fördela släktinformationen på respektive plats.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Petre , d 1693, bosatte sig i Arboga 1656, Jacob 1665.Jacob blev rådman i Arboga 1680 genom kungligt ingripande. Stadens borgare hade velat att någon annan av Arbogas dugliga män blev rådman, någon som ej kom av främmande n
2 CONC ation. Robert Petre senior, som stod vaä anskriven hos Karl XI, lade sig ut för sin brorson i en skrivelse till länsstyrelsen i Örebro. Hans vädjan hörsammades.
2 CONT
2 CONT Det finns också ett kvarter i Arboga vid namn Jakob Petre. Korsningen Räntmästargatan / Nygatan, minst tre arkeologiska gruvschakt är gjorda i kvarteret.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift med Sara Johansdotter, d ca.1680, rådmansdotter från Arboga. De hade sex efterlevande barn varav tre flickor som alla blev bortgifta med banko-tjänstemän. Bröderna hette: Georg, nämns i bouppteckningen 1727 efter systern Elis
2 CONC abeth som "caitain sahl. Petre", men hans namn har inte återfunnits i de svenska rullorna. Welam, var köpman i Stockholm. Samt Robert, yngst av de efterlevande barnen.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Robert Petrie was the son of George Petrie, the provost of Montrose. He was born on 9 September or 1 November 1614 and died 29 March 1690. Robert came to Sweden after his father's death in 1628 or 29 with his brother George [SSNE 
2 CONC 6788] to be with their older brother William [SSNE 6708]. In 1638 he became a burgess of Stockholm. However, he also founded Brattfors steel works in Ockelbo, Gastrickland before moving to Arboga in 1644 where he became both burge
2 CONC ss and district judge. It is presumably this Robert Petrie, noted as 'the elder', who attended the Riksdag in Stockholm in 1668 as a representative for Arboga. Robert married Maria (Mararetha) Hoijer and with her had a son called 
2 CONC Gabriel. According to Hellstrom, his daughter Catharina married William Helleday [SSNE 787]. When Helleday died, sometime in 1679?, Robert took on the service of one John Guthrie [SSNE 2369]who had been in Helleday's service. From
2 CONC  c.1675-1690 Robert Petrie and his sons Robert and Wellam operated Hofors bruk. Wellam continued running this until his own death in 1706. ......................................................................... 
2 CONT Petrus Norberg, 'Gästriklands hyttor och hamrar'in Blad för bergshanteringens vänner (1959). This information, derived from a number of sources, was originally provided by Knut Fasting and updated by Georg Haggren. The information
2 CONC  regarding Helleday and Guthrie comes from G. Hellstrom, Stockholms Stads Herdaminne (Stockholm, 1951), p.436, pp.588-9; Steve Murdoch, Network North: Scottish Kin, Commercial and Covert Associations in Northern Europe, 1603-1746 
2 CONC (Brill, Leiden, 2006), pp.187, 191, 193; Borgarstandets Riksdagsprotokoll, fore Frihetstiden (Uppsala, 1933), p.42.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Petre-113
