2 NOTE The picture shows inscriptions on the wall in the house that Johan van der Hagen owned in the 17th century. Today it is a shop selling old photos ("Old Picture Company"), Västerlånggatan 54 in Old Town (Gamla stan) in Stockholm.
3 CONT According to http://www.tullkust.se/path/om_oss/hushistoria.aspx:
3 CONT
3 CONT In the doorway to the backyard behind present-day Aspington's antiquarian bookseller there are inscriptions 
3 CONT on one side:
3 CONT
3 CONT E:V:D:H: AO
3 CONT 1675 Den 7 may
3 CONT
3 CONT Above later engraved:
3 CONT 1815. 
3 CONT On the other side
3 CONT
3 CONT I.V.D.H
3 CONT L:V:D:HA
3 CONT Ais AO 1681
3 CONT L H I Den 19 sept
3 CONT G V D H
3 CONT A V D H
3 CONT N.D 16 Ao 1684
3 CONT
3 CONT It is obvious that the initials refers to different members of the Hagen family.
